"Flexbox for one direction: a row of buttons, a navbar, centering something. Grid for two dimensions: a gallery or a page skeleton with rows and columns. In practice I combine them: Grid for the page layout and Flexbox inside each component."

```css
.galeria { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(16rem, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; }
.barra { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; }
```

"It means writing styles for small screens first and then adding enhancements with `min-width` queries for larger ones. The CSS ends up simpler and it forces me to prioritize content. On projects like my faculty's portal it makes sense because most visitors are on phones."

```css
.tarjetas { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
@media (min-width: 768px) { .tarjetas { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); } }
```
